  "title": "Shell Scripting for Devops Beginners: Part 2",
  "subtitle": "In this article we revisit some of the most used and most important Linux Commands for interviews, and these Linux commands are also used on a daily basis by every Devops Engineer",
  "date": "2025-11-09",
  "canonical": "https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/p/shell-scripting-for-devops-beginners-626",
  "body_html": "<div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;acfe5767-3631-43b4-a987-2aab816d24f6&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Linux is the backbone of DevOps, cloud engineering, and backend systems. Whether you’re debugging servers, analyzing logs, or writing CI/CD scripts these commands will be your daily tools.&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Read full story&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;sm&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Shell Scripting for Devops Beginners : Part 1&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:327304656,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Pradyumna&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;I write about Software Engineering and AI, breaking down concepts with real-world examples. Subscribe to learn something new every day, from problem statements and scenarios to practical system designs and architecture visuals.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/46130f37-0667-4de2-a1df-4704f08ed96a_1244x1244.png&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:null}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2025-11-07T07:00:09.509Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/c7b05dd5-f87e-46a7-b079-116c75916bbf_1024x1024.png&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/p/shell-scripting-for-devops-beginners&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:178247668,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:1,&quot;comment_count&quot;:0,&quot;publication_id&quot;:6703570,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;LevelYouUp&quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!TLj_!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F46b58d72-63a1-4e35-a4e5-1923ad6c3822_1244x1244.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><div><hr></div><p>Appreciate you reading this newsletter, I hope the content and resources are helping you level up as an engineer. If you want me to write about something specific, just message me or comment on the post.</p><blockquote><p><strong>Note:</strong> This article on was originally published on my blog -<strong> <a href=\"https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/blogs/shell-scripting-part2\">https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/blogs/shell-scripting-part2</a></strong></p></blockquote><div><hr></div><p>In the last article, we learned about some of the basic Linux commands. In this blog post, we will cover Networking Commands, Process Management commands and loops, and conditional operators in Shell scripting, along with some interview questions. </p><p>We forgot to cover a couple of basic commands in the first part, so let’s cover that here and then jump to some cool topics. </p><p>Also learning about Absolute path and relative path, and that’s your homework.<br>Let’s dive right in</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div><ol><li><p><strong>Basic Commands</strong></p><p>Lets look at some basic operators </p><ul><li><p><em>&gt; (overwrite): </em><code>'&gt;‘ </code>sends the output of a command into a file, replacing the file’s existing contents.</p><p>Example : </p><pre><code>echo “hello” &gt; file.txt</code></pre><p>If <code>file.txt</code> exists → it erases everything and replace with <code>“hello”</code></p><p>If it doesn’t exist → <code>file.txt</code> is created with the content “<code>hello”</code></p></li><li><p><code>&gt;&gt;</code><em> (append) : </em><code>‘&gt;&gt;’ </code>sends the output of a command into a file, but adds it at the end, without deleting existing content.</p><p>Example : </p><pre><code>echo “hello” &gt;&gt; file.txt</code></pre><p>If <code>file.txt</code> exists → <code>“hello”</code> is added at the bottom</p><p>If it doesn’t exist → it is created with “hello” in it</p></li></ul></li></ol><p>We will read about other operators like (‘|’) pipe. </p><ol><li><p><strong>Networking Commands </strong></p><pre><code>lsof -i // To check open ports\nping google.com // To check if a host is reachable \nipconfig // to check IP address</code></pre></li><li><p><strong>Process Management</strong></p></li></ol><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1047\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/bb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:1047,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:286440,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/178320084?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!BySu!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fbb60dc97-cdfe-4316-9f1f-f9a910d48fd0_1710x1230.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>The above commands are very important in day-to-day development, especially when debugging slow systems or tracking down resource with heavy usage. </p><ol start=\"3\"><li><p><strong>What is Pipe</strong><code>(|)</code><strong>parameter ?  </strong></p><p>Pipe parameter is used to send the output of the first commands to the second commands. </p><p>if ps -ef returns all the processes then if we do | grep “google” it will give us the processes matching the given “pattern” Google.</p><pre><code>ps -ef | grep \"google\" // returns all lines which matches Google.</code></pre><p>Now, say if i want to retrieve only a specific column after finding the entire matching sentences. Like if i want the pid of the “google” senence then what would you do ? </p><pre><code>ps -ef | awk -F ‘{print $2}’. // will print every pid of all processes\nps -ef | grep \"google\" | awk -F '{print $2}' // prints the pid of only process which have google</code></pre><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div><p><strong>What is awk ?  </strong></p><p><code>awk</code> is a command-line tool and mini programming language for working with text, especially column-based data (like output of <code>ps</code>, <code>df</code>, logs, CSV-ish stuff).</p><pre><code>awk ‘pattern { action }’ file</code></pre></li></ol><ul><li><p>It reads input line by line</p></li><li><p>Splits each line into fields ($1, $2, $3, …)</p></li><li><p>If pattern matches, it runs the { action }</p><p>Say if i want to Print a specific column for example: show only the 1st column of <code>df -h</code>:</p><pre><code><code>df -h | awk ‘{ print $1 }’</code></code></pre><ul><li><p><code>$1</code> → first column</p></li><li><p><code>$2</code> → second column, etc.</p></li><li><p><code>$0</code> → whole line</p></li></ul></li></ul><ol start=\"3\"><li><p><strong>Basic Conditions and Loops </strong></p><p>To understand this, let’s see some interview questions, so that it’’be easier for us to understand hoe these conditional operators and loops work. </p></li></ol><ul><li><p>Print numbers from [1, 30] divisible by 3 </p><pre><code>for i in {1..30}\ndo\n  if [ $((i % 3)) -eq 0 ]\n  then\n    echo “$i is divisible by 3”\n  fi\ndone</code></pre></li><li><p>Without <code>$(( ))</code>Bash will treat numbers as plain text, not math., and </p><pre><code>name=”pradyumna”\necho $name // dollar $ is used for accessing vriable</code></pre><p><code>[ ]</code> is used for conditional checks.</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png\" width=\"428\" height=\"393.5091575091575\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:502,&quot;width&quot;:546,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:428,&quot;bytes&quot;:46979,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/i/178320084?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Uhiy!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb5b11556-1aae-46e9-824b-254a6ee26d78_546x502.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><pre><code>x=1\nwhile [ $x -le 10 ]\ndo\n  echo “Number: $x”\n  x=$((x + 1))\ndone</code></pre></li></ul><ul><li><p>Print the number of ‘S’ in MISSISSIPPI</p><pre><code>echo -n ‘MISSISSIPPI’ |    # print the word (no newline)\ngrep -o ‘S’ |              # extract every ‘S’ and print one per line(purpose of -o)\nwc -l                      # count how many lines = number of S’s</code></pre></li><li><p>Sort a file alphabetically </p><pre><code>sort file.txt</code></pre></li></ul><p>And that’s a wrap. That brings us to the end of the Shell Scripting for DevOps Beginners series.</p><p>These concepts are fundamental for DevOps, SRE, Cloud, and Backend roles.<br>If you found this article helpful, please consider leaving a like and sharing it with your friends. And if you want more such content delivered straight to your inbox, make sure to subscribe.</p><div class=\"subscription-widget-wrap-editor\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://pradyumnachippigiri.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe&quot;,&quot;language&quot;:&quot;en&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"SubscribeWidgetToDOM\"><div class=\"subscription-widget show-subscribe\"><div class=\"preamble\"><p class=\"cta-caption\">Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.</p></div><form class=\"subscription-widget-subscribe\"><input type=\"email\" class=\"email-input\" name=\"email\" placeholder=\"Type your email…\" tabindex=\"-1\"><input type=\"submit\" class=\"button primary\" value=\"Subscribe\"><div class=\"fake-input-wrapper\"><div class=\"fake-input\"></div><div class=\"fake-button\"></div></div></form></div></div>"
}